"Where does the name Taiwan come from? Victor Mair, a scholar of Chinese languages, writes that it comes from the name of an Indigenous people in the southwest of the island. A Dutch ship’s log from 1622 already spelled the area “Teijoan” and “Taiyowan.” On the maps in this lesson, the name is used in two ways, sometimes on the same map: for the whole island (“Tai-ouan ou Isle Formose”) and for one place on the west coast (“Tai-ouan ou Taiwan,” beside a ruined Dutch fort).": "a57cdec52c19",
